OL,3,GNEWSAThe grieving family who say the
OL,4,Acoroners' courts aren't working
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe grieving family who say the
OL,7,Fcoroners' courts aren't working
OL,9,FSarah thought she knew what she was
OL,10,Fgetting into when she attended a
OL,11,Fcoroner's court in May 2024 to discuss
OL,12,Fthe death of her second cousin.
OL,14,FHer day job as a murder detective meant
OL,15,Fshe was used to courts, to judges, to
OL,16,Flegal argument. What she wasn't
OL,17,Fprepared for was a coroner's court. "I
OL,18,Ffelt like I was on trial," she recalls
OL,19,Fof her first hearing, in Woking,
OL,20,FSurrey. "I remember just feeling
OL,21,Fcompletely railroaded... It [was] far
OL,22,Fmore hostile than I had ever expected."
